The first hard asymmetry is now confirmed: OpenCode v2’s path gate is application-level, but `shell` still runs with the host user’s full filesystem/process/network authority and only gates the raw command string plus working directory. That makes its file-tool symlink hardening real but not a shell sandbox. I’m applying the same “actual enforcement, not UI wording” standard to Eve and Flue.
