35-The second subscriber argument: the runtime context of the agent interaction that emitted the event.
36-- `id` — the agent instance id; equals the `instanceId` stamped on the context's events.
37-- `agentName` — the registered agent name, when known.
38-- `env` — platform bindings: `process.env` on Node, the Workers env object on Cloudflare.
39-- `req` — the invocation's Fetch `Request`, or `undefined` outside an HTTP context. Durable or recovered processing may carry a synthetic internal request instead of the original caller request.
40:- `log` — emits [`log` events](#log) into this context's event stream. Calling it from inside a subscriber emits further events; guard against loops.
