73-A create-only send (`uid: null`) — `dispatch()` or `init().dispatch()` with the condition, or the equivalent HTTP body fields — named an instance that already exists. Raised synchronously at admission; nothing durable is created when it fires. Over HTTP it renders with status 409; programmatically the returned promise rejects with the class instance.
74:- `uid` — the existing incarnation's uid, usable directly as the continue condition. `undefined` for instances created before uids shipped. The uid also rides the wire envelope as `meta.uid` (and appears in the `details` prose), so HTTP callers can continue the existing instance without a separate lookup.
75-## `AgentInstanceNotFoundError`
76-```ts
77-class AgentInstanceNotFoundError extends FlueError // type: 'agent_instance_not_found', status: 404
78-```
