201:A terminal error a durable submission settles with: it becomes the `error` of the `submission_settled` record and event (the [settlement error shape](#settlement-error-shape) below) and rejects a waiting settlement observer (`init().read()`, the SDK's `wait()`). Recovery re-attempted an interrupted submission after input application until `durability.maxAttempts` ran out without a completed response; see the [Durability guide](/docs/guide/durability/) for the attempt and timeout model. When terminalization settled tool calls whose outcomes could not be confirmed, `meta.interruptedTools` lists them as `{ name, id }` pairs; each has an explicit interrupted-error outcome in the conversation and was never assumed complete or retried. `meta` also carries `attemptCount` and `maxAttempts`.
